# Ignored paths worktrunk copies into a new worktree.
#
# `.beads/` is deliberately NOT named here, and adding it would be a regression.
#
# Two measurements decide it. First, this file matches top-level entries only: `.beads/`,
# `.beads` and `/.beads/` each resolve to `.beads (dir)` and copy the whole tree, while
# `.beads/*`, `.beads/*.json` and `.beads/**` match nothing. So there is no way to copy the
# connection files without also copying `.beads/dolt/`, which is 2.2MB of Dolt storage a
# worktree must never serve from: if the port file goes stale, that store is exactly what a
# worktree would start a second server on, holding data old enough to look real.
#
# Second, no copy is needed. `bd` resolves its database from `BEADS_DIR`, and from a
# directory holding no `.beads/` at all, `BEADS_DIR=<primary>/.beads bd list` listed this
# run's beads. So `src/beads-mode.ts` resolves the primary checkout's `.beads` through
# `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` and points the run at it. A worktree joins the run's
# server and holds no copy of it.
#
# Nothing else in this repository needs copying: `bun install` is fast and its output is
# reproducible from the lockfile, so a cold worktree costs a install rather than a
# divergent database.
